  <h2>Why we don’t sell perfect source tracking</h2>
  <p>
    Even with serious call-tracking software, a large share of Google-influenced calls never attribute
    cleanly. Homeowners bounce between ads, the website, and the Business Profile. Obsessing over
    which slice “owns” the lead usually produces wrong dashboards and bad budget cuts.
  </p>
  <p>
    Dual-phone shops and missing recordings are mostly a systems problem: modern CRMs and unified
    phone tools (OpenPhone, Quo, and peers) make gaps obvious. We help you use that stack well,
    then judge marketing on calendar bookings and P&amp;L, not a pie chart that lies.
  </p>
